  "notes": "Jive Atlanta soloist in the So So Def / Jazze Pha-orbit crunk-adjacent lane, 2002–2005. The research gives \"64–100 straight; ballads 64–70 half-time\", and the straight band is encoded because five of the eight sourced tempos sit in it and it carries the entry's drum grammar. Three drum deltas from \"Atlanta grammar — 808/909 kick, hard clap on 2&4, 16th hats with triplet fills and a snare-roll pickup into the hook\": `lockTo808` at 0.5 with a real tresillo lean on the kick, a clap stacked within 2 ms of the snare on a dead-flat grid, and — the distinguishing parameter — a hat roll vocabulary weighted onto triplets (`16T`, `32T`) at 0.4 per bar with a velocity ramp, plus a `snareRoll` ladder into the hook. Nothing else in this batch runs triplet hat fills. This is a true 808 model: \"808 sub-bass with a slide into the root, one or two notes per bar, prominent in the mix\" is the whole low end, so `drums.bass808` takes role `bassline` and there is no `bassline` block. Harmony is \"single-chord or two-chord minor vamps with a synth-lead riff as the hook\", so the single-chord family leads and the triad share is high. \"Light nasal alto, chant-forward phrasing, thin doubled harmony\" is the riff-dominant contour, the 3–5 pitch motif and a counter density of 0.36. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ Every velocity, density and ramp number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line. ⚠ **`chords.harmonicRhythm` re-weighted (2026-08-17, harmony variety floor).** The entry gives the one-chord and the two-chord bed equal billing — \"single-chord or two-chord minor vamps with a synth-lead riff as the hook\" — and the engine's `vamp` value is *one* chord held for the whole clip (`generators::chords`: \"One chord for the whole pattern\"), so a `vamp` weight of 6-of-8 made the two-chord half of that sentence almost unreachable. `vamp` keeps the top weight; the two-chord reading is now reachable at both rates. ⚠ The split between those two rates is **INFERRED** — the entry names the device, not its rate.",
